title: Start
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 2
position: -630,120
---
In this example we will look at conditionals in Dialogue Branch.

[[Conditionals]]
===
title: Conditionals
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: -336,119
---
So let's first set some variables that we can use to play with.

<<set $variableThatIsTrue = true>>
<<set $variableThatIsFalse = false>>

[[Conditionals2]]
===
title: Conditionals2
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: -46,117
---
<<if $variableThatIsTrue == true>>
  This statement will only be shown if the variable "variableThatIsTrue" is true (which it is).
<<else>>
  Otherwise, you would see this statement (you will never see this).
<<endif>>

[[Conditionals3]]
===
title: Conditionals3
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 240,116
---
<<if $variableThatIsTrue >>
  You can write the shorthand "if variableName" to check for true (without the "== true" part).
<<endif>>

[[Show me elseif.|ElseIf]]
[[Goodbye.|End]]
===
title: ElseIf
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 240,320
---
<<set $count = 2>>

<<if $count == 1>>
  There is exactly one.
<<elseif $count == 2>>
  There are two of them.
<<else>>
  There are more than two.
<<endif>>

[[Comparisons]]
===
title: Comparisons
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 240,520
---
<<if $count != 1>>
  "not equals" works: $count is not 1.
<<endif>>
<<if $count > 1 >>
  "greater than" works.
<<endif>>
<<if $count < 5 >>
  "less than" works.
<<endif>>
<<if $count >= 2 >>
  "greater or equal" works.
<<endif>>
<<if $count <= 2 >>
  "less or equal" works.
<<endif>>

[[BooleanOps]]
===
title: BooleanOps
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 240,720
---
<<if $variableThatIsTrue && $count == 2>>
  "and" requires both sides to hold.
<<endif>>
<<if $variableThatIsFalse || $count == 2>>
  "or" requires just one side to hold.
<<endif>>

[[Unset]]
===
title: Unset
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 240,920
---
<<if $neverAssigned>>
  You will not see this: the shorthand form treats an unset variable as false.
<<else>>
  The variable $neverAssigned was never assigned, so the shorthand check is false...
<<endif>>
<<if $neverAssigned == false>>
  ...and comparing it to false also matches an unset variable, which can be surprising.
<<endif>>

[[Okay, that is clear.|Conditionals4]]
[[Goodbye.|End]]
===
title: End
tags: 
speaker: 
colorID: 5
position: -224,458
---

===
title: Conditionals4
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 561,118
---
You can make any part of the
<<if $variableThatIsTrue>>
  Dialogue Branch
<<else>>
  NOT DialogueBranch
<<endif>>
dialogue conditional. As long as
<<if $variableThatIsFalse>>
  [[Suddenly a reply option.|End]]
<<else>>
  the resulting contents are valid.
<<endif>>

<<if $variableThatIsFalse >>
  [[The user will never see this reply option.|End]]
<<else>>
  [[Okay, that is clear.|Conditionals5]]
<<endif>>
===
title: Conditionals5
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 870,114
---
<<if $variableThatIsTrue >>
  <<if $variableThatIsFalse >>
    Text that will never be shown.
  <<else>>
    Also, you can nest conditionals as deep as you like.
    <<if $variableThatIsTrue >>
      [[Okay, clear.|Conditionals6]]
    <<endif>>
  <<endif>>
<<else>>
  This text will also never be shown.
<<endif>>
===
title: Conditionals6
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 1186,114
---
Let me set some other variables to show some other things.

<<set $thisIsAString = "Some string.">>
<<set $thisIsANumber = 42>>

[[Okay, show me!|Conditionals7]]
===
title: Conditionals7
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 1499,107
---
<<if $thisIsAString == "Some string." >>
  You can use conditionals using strings or numbers as well, anything you would expect from a scripting language really...
<<endif>>

<<if $thisIsANumber == 42>>
  [[Understood.|Conditionals8]]
<<endif>>
===
title: Conditionals8
tags: 
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorID: 0
position: 1803,110
---
And that's all we have to say about conditionals for today.

[[Thanks and goodbye.|End]]
===
